title: "AquaTrajectories: Aquatic Animal Movement and Multiview Trajectories"
type: software
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-11-15
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24262905"
message: "If you use AquaTrajectories in research or teaching, please cite the software release you used."
authors:
  - family-names: Balaskas
    given-names: Stefanos
    affiliation: University of Patras
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2444-9796"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/stefanosbalaskas/AquaTrajectories"
url: "https://stefanosbalaskas.github.io/AquaTrajectories/"
abstract: >-
  AquaTrajectories is an open-source R and Python research-software toolkit
  for aquatic animal 2D and 3D movement analysis, video-based fish-tracking
  interfaces, multiview reconstruction, camera geometry, behavioural methods,
  conditional uncertainty assessment and reproducible scientific visualization.
  Version 0.1.1 is a published software release with documentation and citation
  metadata. Independently verified fish identities, real-video detection
  generalization, physical underwater XYZ accuracy, animal welfare inference,
  and physical device safety have not been scientifically certified.
keywords:
  - aquatic animal movement
  - fish tracking
  - aquaculture
  - three-dimensional trajectories
  - camera calibration
  - multiview reconstruction
  - behavioural analysis
  - research software
